      "writtenOn": "2026-02-25T17:09:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason these are in `kernel/common` vs `kernel/common-modules/wonder` is so that partners can directly swap in the wonder DDK git project into their kernel tree and use it as-is without the reference wonder kernel_build causing any conflicts. Also, if I move the target definitions to the DDK project, then I would have to add another label flag to define the base_kernel for the wonder kernel build since not all partners use `//common` for the kernel. I believe keeping the reference wonder kernel_build definition outside of the DDK git project is the cleanest approach since it should not be used by anyone except Google.",
      "parentUuid": "c1e2c46b_3e605003",
      "revId": "f2d8540645ba68afafc440508fbd8775dc521b9d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
